# Cross-repo siblings cloned by setup-dev-env at workspace-lock-pinned
# revisions. They are io-mon's `uses:` library producers in repro.nim
# (reprobuild builds each from source and threads its `src/` root onto
# io-mon's compile); they are also the `--path` siblings config.nims
# resolves for the plain `nim c` / `nimble` build.
#
# nim-stackable-hooks is a bare name: `clone-siblings` resolves it from this
# commit's own committed `repro.lock` (`lock-store: committed`, reprobuild-pm
# Unified-Locking-And-Hooks.md §14.5), which pins 3af63af — the same revision
# `flake.nix` pins `stackable-hooks-src` to. Keep the two in step: a `nim c` in
# the dev shell resolves `stackable_hooks/...` through the sibling checkout,
# while `nix build .#default` resolves it through the flake input, and a build
# that disagrees about which nim-stackable-hooks it is compiling against is the
# failure this file exists to prevent.
#
# It carried an acknowledged override ('!=a043a07') until the two locks agreed.
# The record-store lock `clone-siblings` used to read had frozen the pin at
# 25bf49e4 (a forward carry by the since-retired `publish-workspace-lock.yml`),
# which predates 6a53408 ("Windows injector: an explicit child environment"),
# where `src/stackable_hooks/windows_env_block.nim` arrived; so
# `tests/portable/test_io_mon_windows_child_env_block.nim` could not compile in
# CI ("cannot open file: stackable_hooks/windows_env_block") and `nimble test`
# stopped there. The override was then kept while the committed `repro.lock`
# pinned bb01d793, a descendant of a043a07, rather than the flake's revision.
nim-stackable-hooks
nim-shm-queue

# nim-shm-gset is required by `src/io_mon/writer.nim` (`import
# shm_gset/transport`) and by scripts/build_shim.sh, but it was missing from
# this list, so `just build` failed with "missing nim-shm-gset at
# ../nim-shm-gset/src" and `just test` with "cannot open file:
# shm_gset/transport". Both were reported as PASSING jobs, because those
# steps pipe into `tee` and the default `run` shell has no pipefail; ci.yml
# now sets `shell: bash` so the exit status survives.
#
# Pinned to an explicit revision rather than resolved from the lock: the lock
# CI reads, this commit's committed `repro.lock` (see above), pins only
# io-mon, nim-shm-queue and nim-stackable-hooks — its `deps` are io-mon's
# develop set, and nim-shm-gset is not in it — so a bare `nim-shm-gset` entry
# would be a named refusal instead of a clone. (The io-mon records published
# to metacraft-manifests, 8b6d0b9b and ea5fa77a, which CI read before, had the
# same gap.) The durable fix is to add nim-shm-gset to io-mon's develop set
# (its `depends` edges in the workspace manifest), so `repro lock refresh`
# pins it alongside its siblings; this pin should be dropped then.
# 43a61120 is the revision `flake.nix` pins `shm-gset-src` to, so the
# ordinary checkout and `nix build .#default` compile the same nim-shm-gset
# (keep the two in step, as for nim-stackable-hooks above).
#
# Spelled '!=' rather than '='. It was added when a record-store lock did pin
# nim-shm-gset (at 8a9f2f13), which made a plain '=' an unacknowledged
# override that `clone-siblings` warned about on every run. The committed
# `repro.lock` pins nothing for nim-shm-gset, so today the '!=' acknowledges
# nothing: `clone-siblings` reports this entry as `explicit` ("the lock does not
# pin this repo"), and '!=' and '=' behave identically. Once the lock pins it,
# drop this entry as the paragraph above says, rather than keep an
# acknowledged override.
nim-shm-gset!=43a61120ae54b542c3e3038453094cca707a6c05
